<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14835" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀργύριον</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ], τό,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>small coin, piece of money,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				262
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Oec.</u>
				19.16
			</span></i>, etc.: pl. (v. <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				9.89
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				600
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eup.
				155
			</span></i>, X.l.c.: then, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			collectively, <i>money,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				156
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				158
			</span></i>, al.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ῥητόν</span> a fixed
				<i>sum,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.70
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς ἀ. λογισθέντα</span>
			calculated in <i>our money,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				3.1.33
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. καθαρόν</span> 'hard
			<i>cash</i>', <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				15.36
			</span></i>: in Com. with Art., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τἀργύριον</span>
			<i>the money, the cash,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δανείζεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Nu.</u>
					756
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπαιτεῖν</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				1247
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατατιθέναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antiph.
					124.14
				</span></i>
			, etc.; so 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τἀ. καταβάλλειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					1.27
				</span></i>
			, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄργυρος</span>
			, <i>silver,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεντηκοσίας μνέας ἀργυρίου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					3.13
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἐπίσημον</span> and 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄσημον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					2.13
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρυσίον καὶ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Alc.</u>
					1.122e
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀργυρίου ἄνθος</span>”
				<i>lead oxide,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Nat.Mul.</u>
					33
				</span></i>
			.</div>
